{#-
    1.29 (Beacon spec 234): what follows a message author's name on the full chat page (page.html.twig): the
    application's badges (ChatAuthorBadgeProviderInterface), each printed escaped (never HTML
    from the application), with a class per allow-listed variant. Included only for authors that have badges, so a host
    without a provider renders exactly what 1.28 rendered.

    To draw them differently, create templates/bundles/NowoChatKitBundle/_author_badges.html.twig, extend
    '@!NowoChatKitBundle/_author_badges.html.twig' and redefine the block nowo_chat_author_badges (see USAGE). The dock
    draws its badges from the `author-badge` <template> of _templates.html.twig (block nowo_chat_template_author_badge).

    Included with with_context = false. Variables: badges (non-empty list of {label, variant, title}).
-#}
{%- block nowo_chat_author_badges -%}
    {%- for badge in badges %} <span class="nowo-chat-author-badge nowo-chat-author-badge--{{ badge.variant }}" data-variant="{{ badge.variant }}"{% if badge.title %} title="{{ badge.title }}"{% endif %}>{{ badge.label }}</span>{% endfor -%}
{%- endblock -%}
